meanings=[
 ('SKY01','The complete optional SHADOWSKY record has TypeSHADOW, Status, Accuracy100, TotalPP0, BothSides, StartShadowSkyWeather and CanProtect; Power omission supplies0. BothSides has0ordinary targets, and the inherited ordinary add-target does not invent targets. General effect still requires all actual earlier use/failure gates.','WP45§4.4 / existing fourTarget packet'),
 ('SKY02','StartShadowSkyWeather inherits the whole WeatherMove failure gate: stored HarshSun/HeavyRain/StrongWinds or alreadyShadowSky fails, even when effective weather is suppressed toNone. Stored ordinary orNone can pass that gate.','WP45§4.4'),
 ('SKY03','Its reached General calls pbStartWeather(user,ShadowSky,true,false): fixed duration requested, no duplicate generic start animation from that argument. Ability hiding/weather-specific message/form checks still follow if earlier calls return normally.','WP45§4.1/4.4'),
 ('SKY04','The weather core returns immediately for identical raw stored weather, without refreshing duration or notifying. Otherwise it writes new weather before computing/extending local duration. This direct core gate is separate from the move parent gate.','WP45§4.1'),
 ('SKY05','For fixedtrue local duration starts5. Positive duration and a source with active held item invokes WeatherExtender; only four default registrations exist in the actually read group, each matching Rain/Sun/Hail/Sandstorm. Their ShadowSky nil results fall back to input5. Their exact four complete Itemrecords are included; no held-rock consumption occurs in this callback.','WP45§4.1/4.4'),
 ('SKY06','pbWeather asks living battlers for active CloudNine/AirLock; effectiveNone does not mutate raw weather/duration. Battler effectiveWeather then masks only theSun/Rain pair with active UtilityUmbrella; ShadowSky itself is outside that mask. Effective ability/item checks preserve faint/GastroAcid/NeutralizingGas and Embargo/MagicRoom/corrosiveGas/Klutz gates.','WP45§3.2'),
 ('SKY07','A reached weather end-round stage decrements positive duration before effective effects, including while weather is suppressed;-1 does not decrement. This local counter rule does not promise the battle reaches five later stages.','WP45§4.3'),
 ('SKY08','On duration reaching0, end message precedes rawNone write, then forms, then a nonNone default is started with no fixedtrue/user, hence-1. If raw weather remainsNone the stage returns; a restarted default continues its own feedback/ability/damage in this same stage. No saved temporary-weather stack is resumed.','WP45§4.3'),
 ('SKY09','ShadowSky weather damage requires a living target and its effectiveWeatherShadowSky. takesShadowSkyDamage? additionally requires the common indirect-damage gate (active MagicGuard rejects) and Pokemon Shadow flag false. Species ordinary type alone does not supply Shadow immunity.','WP45§4.3'),
 ('SKY10','Nominal weather amount is integer totalhp/16; reached pbReduceHP rounds/caps tocurrentHP and raises the amount to1 if below1 whilealive. The Battle hp setter also writes the referenced Pokemon hp; Pokemon zeroHP clears status/readiness. The nominal quotient is not automatically the eventual post-item HP delta.','WP45§4.3 / existing HP contract'),
 ('SKY11','Weather message and damage animation occur before the HP-reduction call. Within pbReduceHP, hp writes precede its log/bounds/HPchanged callback and damage flags. On normal return the weather caller asks itemHPHealCheck, then Faint ifstillfainted; any later failure retains the reached prefix. Item callback or faint outcomes are not assumed universally.','WP45§4.3 / existing finite CORE choice/faint receipt'),
 ('SKY12','All five complete EndOfRoundWeather registrations (DrySkin,IceBody,IceFace,RainDish,SolarPower) were actually read. None executes its body branch for effectiveShadowSky orNone. Restoring a different default before this stage can enable its respective nonShadow branch; later EndOfRoundHealing is a separate group.','Finite ShadowSky/None callback classification, not all ability callbacks'),
 ('SKY13','Weather form checks may commit actual Pokemon forms: living nonTransform ForecastCastform/FlowerGiftCherrim choose0 underShadowSky/None; Eiscue restore flag requires Hail. pbChangeForm writes via Battler.form= toPokemon.form, then full pbUpdate copies current Pokemon types/ability. A previous battle-onlyShadow type copy can therefore be replaced while the Pokemon Shadow flag remains; no all-form or purevisual claim.','WP45§4.1; existing WP21/WP23'),
 ('SKY14','In the complete damage-multiplier method, the weather branch reads the user effectiveWeather; ShadowSky multiplies final-damage multiplier by1.5 only when the current calculated type argument isSHADOW. This is one factor among the real earlier/later gates and multipliers, not an executed final-damage result.','WP43 damage weather row135'),
 ('SKY15','BattleWeather is a hardcoded9-ID registry, not a PBS Type registry. Its constructor retainsid/name/animation, and load/save are noops; animationShadowSky is an animation identity request. Initial names are passed throughINTL at registration and name getter again, so no observed localized word or native animation is inferred.','WP45§2 domain; source typed metadata only'),
 ('SKY16','Weather ability wrapper and direct default setter remain distinct consumers: default setter writes default/current/-1 directly; ordinary ability wrapper guards stored primal andsameweather, derives fixed duration from config, then calls core. ShadowSky move instead uses its own fixedtrue caller, not this ability-duration policy.','WP45§3/4.1'),
 ('SKY17','The precise weather failure prefix matters: new raw weather is written before the extendercallback, while duration is stored only after that callback returns. Animation/hide/message/forms/primordialcheck follow theduration write. Thus extender failure can leave newweather with previousduration; latermessage/form failure leaves earlierwrites. No rollback or native/game/compiled/save execution is implied.','WP45§4.4 prefix and correct generic source ordering')]
